  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A = (2 3 / −1 4) and x is the column vector (5 / 2). (a) Calculate the matrix product Ax. (b) State the order of Ax."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Multiplying a 2 × 2 matrix by a column vector gives another column vector: each row of A meets the single column of x."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p198_q09.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p198-q09 from workbook page 198."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Check the product is defined.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(2 × 2)(2 × 1): the inner numbers are both 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Ax is defined, order 2 × 1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Multiply row 1 of A into the column x.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 × 5 + 3 × 2 = 10 + 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Top entry = 16"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Multiply row 2 of A into the column x.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "−1 × 5 + 4 × 2 = −5 + 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Bottom entry = 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Assemble the answer as a column vector.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Two rows, one column."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Ax = (16 / 3)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Multiply each row of A into the column x, adding the products, then read the order from the outer numbers 2 and 1."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) Ax = (16 / 3), that is the column vector with entries 16 and 3  (b) The order of Ax is 2 × 1"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Each entry of the product comes from pairing a row of the first matrix with a column of the second, multiplying matched entries and adding. Because x has only one column, the answer also has only one column, so the shape 2 × 1 is forced by the rule that the outer numbers survive. This is exactly the structure that lets a matrix equation stand for simultaneous equations."
    }
  ],
